          "text": "**JSON Construction: Amide Coupling Optimization**\n\nOkay, I've got all the SMILES and I'm ready to build the JSON. First, a quick sanity check to make sure I'm not missing anything crucial. I've re-read entry 13's footnote 'd' again, just to be absolutely certain. Yes, it confirms the control experiment: \"Reaction without 2\". That's key; it means reactant 2 (ethylenediamine) is omitted in this entry.\n\nNow, let's review: I've confirmed entry 13 is missing reagent 2.\n\nThe table represents the optimization of reaction conditions for an amide coupling. We have thirteen entries. The core reaction is 1 + 2 -> 3. The general scheme is clear: 1 (Boc-protected amino acid) reacts with 2 (ethylenediamine) to give 3 (amide product). I've got the reactants and products down with their SMILES strings, and I've verified the wildcard versions with `R` as `[1*]`.\n\nThe key experimental parameters are: catalyst (A, B, C, D at 5 mol%), solvent (toluene, THF, DCE, CPME, DMF), temperature (60 or 80 \u00b0C), and reaction time (12 h). Substrate 1a (Boc-Gly-OH) is used in entry 1, and 1b (Boc-Ala-OH) is used for all remaining entries. I've also checked the loadings: 1 (0.20 mmol), 2 (1.5 equiv), and 5 mol% catalyst.\n\nI\u2019ve verified all catalyst names and I've double checked the solvent structures with their SMILES and they are all correct.\n\nRegarding the yields, I've noted that the yields reported are by NMR. I also saw that for entry 6, we have a NMR yield of 96% and an isolated yield of 91%. So, the JSON will need both a `yield_pct` and `yield_note` to fully capture that result.\n\nI've also confirmed all the yields, noted the superscripts, the reactants and products of all the entries, all catalysts, and all solvents.\n\nI've double-checked the loadings of everything.\n\nOkay, I think I'm ready to construct the JSON.\n\n\n"
